{"reviews":[{"id":"B001V9V71U-0","r":5.0,"t":"Good drops for sore, dry, scratchy eyes","x":"My eye doctor recommended these drops to me many years ago when I complained about dry, scratchy eyes. He told me to use these until the soreness/scratchiness went away, and to continue to use regular eye drops to keep my eyes from getting dry. I continued to use them from time to time over the years whenever I encountered the same problem.  They are pricey, and at one point I did buy a store brand (I think it was from Walgreens), and they seemed to work as well. I think the price of these drops","h":13,"v":1,"d":"Nov 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-1","r":5.0,"t":"Muro 128 5%","x":"I have a cornea degenerative disease (Fuchs Dystrophy) in both eyes, and have had to use these eye drops for several years.  They do exactly what they were designed to do, which is take the fluid out of the cornea in order to see better.  I will use these drops (Muro 128 5%) forever.","h":12,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-2","r":4.0,"t":"Fuchs' Dystrophy","x":"I just had cataract surgery and found out I have Fuch's disease. I use them to try to get the excess fluid out of my corneas.  They sting but I have high hopes they will take some of the swelling down.","h":12,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2018"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-3","r":5.0,"t":"Works for me.","x":"I recently had cataract surgery in both eyes. One was worse than the other and I was told to get this to help the swelling in my eye. I had to end up ordering this on line as no place had it. It does sting a second or two but it does the job! It helped the swelling go down and also took away any soreness I had after the surgery on my one eye.","h":10,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-4","r":5.0,"t":"Expensive, but very effective relief from Fuch's Dystrophe","x":"Fuch's Dystrophe is a chronic swelling of the corneas that causes one's eyes to be almost constantly irritated and sore. It is not a dangerous medical condition, bit it is awfully uncomfortable and annoying. I tried Muro 123 5% at my optometrist's recommendation, and results have been good.  Regular eye drops do provide some relief from the \"scratchy\" feel by lubricating the surface of the eye, but little more. Muro 128 5% actually reduces the swelling of the cornea for an hour or two after each","h":8,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-5","r":4.0,"t":"Muro 128 was helped me with my problem with Fuchs Dystrophy","x":"I have been using Muro 128 for the last three years.  It has helped with my Fuchs Dystrophy.  I made the mistake of thinking that I was buying the 1 oz bottle when I actually ordered the .5 oz size so I was disappointed when it arrived.  However, I will use it anyway.","h":8,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2013"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-6","r":5.0,"t":"Will burn.","x":"This is a salt bath for your eye it will sting and has no smell to it that\u2019s why 1 stars on those questions. Great price will last you a month and a half depending on how often you use it.","h":8,"v":1,"d":"May 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-7","r":5.0,"t":"Do the job nicely","x":"The drops do exactly what I purchased them for, but they aren\u2019t cheap anywhere I\u2019ve looked, and a 5% saline eye drop does burn.  It isn\u2019t agonizing of course, but do be prepared.","h":8,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-8","r":5.0,"t":"MURO 128 5%","x":"Works well Arrived as expected. Use it for my dog's dry eyes","h":8,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-9","r":1.0,"t":"expiration date?","x":"NOOOO!  Don't waste money.  product was old and dropper was always clogged","h":6,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2018"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-10","r":5.0,"t":"Great for Dry Eye","x":"I used after cataract surgery. My wife has RA and associated dry eye. Works better than any other drops, gels. etc she has used.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Nov 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-11","r":5.0,"t":"Great for Dry Eye","x":"I used after cataract surgery. My wife has RA and associated dry eye. Works better than any other drops, gels. etc she has used.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Nov 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-12","r":4.0,"t":"Works","x":"Works But rediculously overpriced, maybe just me not used with such","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2018"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-13","r":5.0,"t":"My doctor recommended this.","x":"My eye doctor recommends this for my dry eye. Ordering from Amazon was so convenient. Local pharmacies rarely has this in stock.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-14","r":4.0,"t":"muro 128 5% ointment","x":"The product itself was exactly what I expected it to be.  However, the 2 boxes containing the tube of Muro 128 Ointment 5% did not have the seal which normally has to be torn or cut which was a bit concerning to me.  While the product was fine, not having that seal made me feel that the product was not totally tamper proof.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-15","r":5.0,"t":"Good product for extreme dry eyes","x":"This somehow works to reduce swelling and reduce water in the eyes. It burns for about 20 seconds but there is relief. I\u2019m young and have extreme dry eyes mainly at night so bad that my eye lids stick to my eyeball. I\u2019ve been to multiple specialists and they have no idea what it could be. But this provides some relief.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"May 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-16","r":5.0,"t":"Seems to work","x":"My eye doctor told me to use Muro 128 and I followed his advice.  It was a bit difficult to find but I did find it on Amazon.  It arrived very quickly and at a reasonable price.  I presume it is working.  I will find out when I go back for a follow-up visit.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2020"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-17","r":5.0,"t":"If you have dry eye, please consult a specialist, Opthalmologist , M.D. for correct diagnosis.","x":"I disliked this product because it burns like crazy when you put it in your eyes, but the burning only lasts for a minute or two. I liked these eye drops because they seem to be working to help my eye condition from getting any worse.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2021"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-18","r":5.0,"t":"Great product","x":"My doctor told me to buy these for my eyes. They help my dry eyes, and they are easy to get from Amazon. Also, with my Prime membership, they are cheaper to buy than in a local store.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-19","r":5.0,"t":"Recommended by Optometrist","x":"This product was recommended to me for cornea edema by the optometrist. He said to use the eye drops twice a day. They burn slightly for few seconds and make the eyes water.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2019"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-20","r":4.0,"t":"cost and valve","x":"I ordered the wrong Muro 128 was wanting the ointment not solution. Solution has a slight burning when you put on eyes doesn't last that long and burning goes away.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Jan 2020"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-21","r":5.0,"t":"This product helps keep my little dog from being in extreme pain","x":"My dog has fluid on the corneas of his eyes. This product keeps the fluid from blistering and bursting which would cas tremendous pain","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Oct 2020"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-22","r":5.0,"t":"They were prescribed by my optometrist.  Due to edema on my eye.","x":"I had some edema on one eye due to low pressure.  These were available through Amazon and delivered in a timely manner.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2022"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-23","r":1.0,"t":"Not for me...","x":"My doctor recommended these for chronic dry eyes, but my eyes burn when I use this product, so disappointing.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2020"},{"id":"B001V9V71U-24","r":5.0,"t":"Does the job","x":"Clears up my vision nicely, including dry eye. Slight burning but my eye doctor steered me the right way.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2021"}],"emb":"","summary":{"claims":[{"text":"Many reviewers report the drops effectively relieve dry, scratchy, sore eyes and reduce corneal swelling, often on a doctor's recommendation.","cites":[1,2,4,5,11,12,14]},{"text":"Several reviewers note the drops sting or burn, though most say it is brief and worth it for the relief.","cites":[3,4,7,8]},{"text":"A common complaint is that the product is expensive or overpriced.","cites":[5,8,13]},{"text":"Some reviewers mention packaging or quality issues, such as a clogged dropper, old product, missing seals, or receiving a smaller size than expected.","cites":[6,10,15]},{"text":"Multiple reviewers use the drops for Fuchs' Dystrophy or after cataract surgery and report good results.","cites":[2,3,4,5,6,11,12]}]},"qa":[]}